            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a blanket, then the Telugu for a curtain, a screen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: తాళం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తాళం — tāḷaṁ — \"a lock\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తాళం (tāḷaṁ) is native Dravidian, one word with Tamil tāḻ and Kannada tāḻ, \"bolt, bar\" (DEDR 3179), which lists tāḷamu, \"lock, key\". DEDR compares Sanskrit tāla and tāḍaka, \"latch, bolt\" (CDIAL 5749)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
